\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1 Their names are names of kings 
\par Of heavenly line;
\par The bliss of earthly things 
\par They did resign.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2 Chieftains they were, who warred 
\par With sword and shield;
\par Victors for God the Lord 
\par On foughten field.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3 Sad were their days on earth,
\par Mid hate and scorn,
\par A life of pleasures dearth, 
\par A death forlorn;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4 Yet blest that end in woe,
\par  And those sad days;
\par Only mans blame below;
\par Above-Gods praise.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5 A city of great name
\par Is built for them, 
\par Of glorious golden fame-
\par Jerusalem! 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6 Redeemed with precious blood 
\par From death and sin,
\par Sons of the Triune God, 
\par They enter in.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7 So doth the life of pain 
\par In glory close;
\par Lord God, may we attain 
\par Their Grand repose.   Amen
\par 
\par 
